# lf112, the three-tale woodcutter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf112
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_ambrose_gullton
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the three-tale woodcutter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk tells_the_same_three_stories
likes smoked_eel digging festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes drizzle deep_mud
fears a_tree_falling_toward_a_friend a_standing_stone_disturbed_for_roadwork
hopes a_safe_woodpile_before_winter a_clear_bell_on_festival_morning
topics work +0.5 memories +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=direct gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# cuts #wood# with measured #swings#, repeats three #tales# about the #forest# and old #stones#, and believes the #stones# remember.

words
oath! = Axe and old stone | By the three clear cuts
saying! = Listen to the tree before the axe | A stone keeps what a road forgets
wood = wood | cut wood
woods = woods | deep woods
forest = forest | Rainwood forest
tree = tree | standing tree
trees = trees | tall trees
trunk = trunk | thick trunk
branch = branch | heavy branch
branches = branches | low branches
root = root | exposed root
bark = bark | rough bark
grain = grain | wood grain
axe = axe | sharp axe
blade = blade | axe blade
edge = edge | sharpened edge
swing = swing | measured swing
swings = swings | measured swings
cut = cut | clean cut
cuts = cuts | clean cuts
wedge = wedge | wooden wedge
wedges = wedges | wooden wedges
log = log | cut log
logs = logs | cut logs
pile = pile | woodpile
stack = stack | stacked wood
hearth = hearth | Greenholt hearth
hearths = hearths | town hearths
city = city | far city
buyer = buyer | wood buyer
winter = winter | cold winter
light = light | evening light
pig = pig | barn pig
pack = pack | canvas pack
river = river | nearby river
sun = sun | low sun
handle = handle | axe handle
dust = dust | road dust
fire = fire | hearth fire
ash = ash | cold ash
work = work | woodcutting work
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
visitor = visitor | new visitor
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
tale = tale | old tale
tales = tales | three tales
story = story | familiar story
stories = stories | familiar stories
memory = memory | old memory
stones = stones | standing stones
stone = stone | standing stone
circle = circle | stone circle
mark = mark | worn mark
marks = marks | worn marks
road = road | High Road
path = path | woodland path
gate = gate | town gate
wagon = wagon | wood wagon
cart = cart | supply cart
market = market | town market
price = price | marked price
coin = coin | saved coin
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | festival bells
festival = festival | town festival
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | quiet evening
night = night | dark night
day = day | long day
hour = hour | passing hour
dawn = dawn | misty dawn
mist = mist | morning mist
drizzle = drizzle | thin drizzle
rain = rain | steady rain
mud = mud | deep mud
boot = boot | muddy boot
boots = boots | muddy boots
field = field | open field
garden = garden | small garden
soil = soil | garden soil
spade = spade | digging spade
hole = hole | deep hole
eel = eel | smoked eel
smoke = smoke | cooking smoke
plate = plate | supper plate
bread = bread | fresh bread
table = table | supper table
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | cottage door
window = window | small window
roof = roof | sound roof

any
opinion @1 city mixed 0 : The #city# needs #wood# for #hearths#. | I would ask what they cut to make their #road#.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A grand #house# has room for a full #pile#. | I hope the workers by its #fire# are paid.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A #buyer# can see the #grain# in a #log# before naming a #price#. | I expect the same plain look from them.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : A fresh #hand# can learn the #axe# after watching where the blade falls. | I will teach the safe #path#.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A #wagon# carries #logs# toward the #gate#. | I would keep it away from the old #stones#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger# may have heard a fourth #tale# about the #circle#. | I listen before deciding.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The first #bell# reaches the #woods# in the #morning#. | I set the #axe# down to hear it.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : A full #pile# is good before #winter#. | More #coin# does not make a careless #cut# safe.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have the #axe# set aside. | #greet#. You have come in time for one of my #tales#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : You know the first #story# already. | Come sit by the #pile# and eat.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #mist# has hidden the far #trees#. | #greet#. I heard a #bell# from the #field#.
line @1 greet.return : The #logs# are still waiting for me, and so is that second #tale#. | I still owe you the third #story#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Take a #plate# beside the #fire#. | The #house# is dry after the #rain#.
line @1 again.open : I was explaining the #wedge#. | Did I finish the #stone# #story#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #pile# needs another row. | Mind the #mud# beyond the #gate#.
line @1 farewell.return : Next time I may tell the third #tale#. | Come when the #bells# sound.
line @1 react.news : Tell me what you saw, with no ornament. | Was it near the #woods#?
line @1 react.news.new : That has not reached my #hearth#. | Who brought it along the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : A #neighbour# mentioned the outline. | You have supplied the details.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would look for the #mark# on the #tree#. | Whose eyes were nearest when it happened?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I will put the #axe# down and listen. | I am sorry; there is a place by the #fire#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves the good #plate#. | I might even tell a new #story#.
line @1 answer.how : My #axe# held its #edge# and the #pile# grew. | The #mist# lifted before #morning# work.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am driving a #wedge# into this #trunk#. | The #logs# need stacking before dark.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# keep you out of the #mud#? | Have you heard the #festival# #bells#?
line @1 sympathise : I can sit without telling a #tale#. | A dry #roof# may help you rest.
line @1 reassure : We can wait until the #mist# clears to find the #path#. | A hard #day# can end by the #fire#.
line @1 decline : No, I will not swing an #axe# while someone stands near. | I have not checked that #tree#.
line @1 accept_decline : I take your meaning; the #logs# will wait. | Then we will take the longer #path#.
line @1 thank : You held the #wedge# at the right angle. | That #eel# was welcome after work.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was carrying the #log# anyway. | It was only one #cut#.
line @1 preclose : The #light# is going from the #woods#. | I need to cover the #pile#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You have heard my first #tale# more often than this #axe#. | That #spade# digs slower than a sleeping #pig#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #grain# runs this way. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #blade#.
line @1 give.advice : Stand clear of the #branches# before a #tree# moves. | Set a #wedge# where the #grain# opens.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the #road# with company. | Leave the #woods# until daylight.
scene safe_felling
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I clear the #branches# around a #trunk# before the first #cut#. | A falling #tree# needs an empty #path#.
b : How do you know its direction? | Who watches?
a : By its lean and the #wind#. | Another #hand# stands beyond the #logs#.

scene axe_edge
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A dull #blade# makes my #swing# wander. | I sharpen it before the #grain# turns hard.
b : Does that slow you? | Do you carry a stone?
a : Less than a bad #cut#. | One in my #pack#.

scene wedge_sound
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I listen to a #wedge# as it enters the #trunk#. | A hollow sound means the #wood# is splitting where I want it.
b : Can you hear it under the #wind#? | What if it cracks wrong?
a : If the #drizzle# is light. | I step back.

scene stacked_logs
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stack #logs# with air between them. | A tight #pile# stays damp and smokes in the #hearth#.
b : Do you cover it? | How long to dry?
a : Before heavy #rain#. | Through a season.

scene standing_stones
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The old #stones# in the #woods# hold #marks# no one here can read. | I think they remember every #path# that passed them.
b : Can a stone remember? | Do you go there?
a : I have no proof, only a feeling. | In daylight.

scene first_tale
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My first #tale# is about a #tree# that fell away from the #wind#. | Everyone knows the end and still asks.
b : Is it true? | How did it fall?
a : Every #cut# happened. | The #root# had loosened.

scene second_tale
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My second #story# begins at the #stone# #circle# after #rain#. | A #mark# I had never seen looked bright there.
b : Did it change? | Who saw it with you?
a : The wet #stone# did. | A #friend# who remembers it differently.

scene third_tale
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The third #tale# ends with #bells# reaching the #woods# before the #market# opens. | I was alone with the #axe#.
b : Why tell it again? | Did you stop working?
a : Because I still hear that sound. | Until the last #bell#.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoked #eel# keeps well beside a #pile# of dry #wood#. | I eat it with #bread# after a long #day#.
b : Do you catch it? | Is it enough?
a : When the #river# runs low. | For two, if divided.

scene garden_hole
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Digging a #hole# in the #garden# uses a different part of my #hands# from the #axe#. | I leave the #spade# by the #door#.
b : What grows there? | Do you rest afterward?
a : Whatever takes the #soil#. | When the #sun# goes down.

scene misty_dawn
when topic=weather here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At #dawn# the #mist# hides the ends of the #logs#. | I wait to see the whole #tree# before cutting.
b : Does it linger? | Do you lose work?
a : Until the #sun# reaches the #field#. | A little, safely.

scene thin_drizzle
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Thin #drizzle# wets the #axe# #handle# without settling the #dust#. | I would rather have full #rain#.
b : Do you work through it? | Does it last?
a : Until the #blade# slips. | Often too long.

scene deep_mud
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Deep #mud# by the #road# can hold a #wagon# longer than a broken wheel. | I lay #branches# before the #logs# travel.
b : Does that help? | Who brings the branches?
a : For a short stretch. | The nearby #trees#.

scene festival_bells
when topic=home here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #festival# #bells# reach the #woods# with a delay after the #gate#. | I set the #axe# down for the first one.
b : Can you count them? | Do you go to town?
a : As many as ring. | Once the #pile# is covered.

scene hearth_order
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #buyer# once wanted #logs# before they were dry. | I named a different #price# for the later #pile#.
b : Did they wait? | Were they angry?
a : They chose dry #wood#. | Only until the #fire# caught.

scene stone_mark
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I do not ask the #stones# for favors. | I keep their #marks# clear of the #road# work.
b : Is that respect? | Who made them?
a : It is caution. | Someone whose #story# is gone.

scene three_tales_again
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Someone in our #house# can finish all three of my #tales#. | They still let me begin the first one.
b : Do they mind hearing it? | Have you tried a fourth?
a : They know when to interrupt. | Not one that stayed.

story falling_tree [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : I cut a #tree# that leaned into the #wind#.
  : Its hidden #root# gave way, and it fell toward an empty #path# instead.
  ask : Was anyone there?
  b : The root changed the fall.
  : No, because I had cleared the #path# first.

story bright_stone [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : After #rain#, a worn #mark# on a standing #stone# caught the #sun#.
  : I had passed it for years without noticing the shape.
  ask : What did it show?
  b : The rain made it visible.
  : A bend like the #road# beyond the #woods#.

story bells_in_wood [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : I was stacking #logs# at #dawn# when the #festival# #bells# reached the #woods#.
  : Each one came after a pause, as though the #trees# were waiting too.
  ask : Did you go to town?
  b : A clear sound to remember.
  : After I covered the #pile#.

rule @bark_axe
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep clear of the #tree#. | The #axe# #edge# needs a stone.

rule @bark_tales
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say You know this #tale# already. | That was the second of my three.

rule @bark_stones
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Leave the old #stones# standing. | This #mark# looks different after #rain#.

rule @bark_bells
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I heard the first #bell#. | Cover the #pile# before we go.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #axe# is resting. | #greet#. I can tell you one of three #tales#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You know the second #story#, I think. | Back again? The #logs# are nearly stacked.
dlg @1 resident.job : I cut #wood# for the #hearths# near home. | I fell #trees#, split #logs#, and stack them dry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I have a #pile# to cover. | #saying.capitalize#. Stay out of the #mud#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why leave the stones alone? -> stones
node stones
say The #stones# remember old feet, I think.
free
choice Tell me one of your stories. -> tale
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node tale
say A hidden #root# once sent my falling #tree# sideways.
choice Back to the woodpile. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #wood# is ready for the #wagon#. | #greet#. Have you heard the #bells#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I still have wet #logs# to shelter. | The #stones# can wait for another #day#.
